        "caption": "Taymar Spencer",
        "label": "",
        "heading": "",
        "body": "<p>Rizo didn’t start with some perfect mission. I started it because I wanted to prove something to myself. I needed something I could offer people, and I wanted to see if I could build it.</p><p>Then people started holding me accountable. A print peeled. Somebody was disappointed. I made bad choices. I learned. Somebody would support me harder than I expected and I’d want to surprise them with something extra.</p><p>Somewhere in there, the reason changed. What started as me trying to get value from people turned into me trying to give value back. Rizo became my passion without me deciding it would.</p>",
